# UI/UX & Responsiveness Optimization Plan

This plan aims to optimize the overall User Interface (UI) and User Experience (UX) across the SkillArena platform by standardizing margins, paddings, and ensuring all components look excellent on mobile devices.

## Open Questions
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Since this is a broad request, are there **specific pages** or components (e.g., the Leaderboard, Course Builder, or Mobile Navbar) where you noticed things looking broken or misaligned? If so, please let me know so I can prioritize them!

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Global Spacing & Typography (Fluid Design)
Instead of static margin/padding values, we will introduce fluid spacing.
#### [MODIFY] `variables.css`
- Convert static `--space-*` variables (like `16px`, `24px`) to `clamp()` functions so they automatically shrink on smaller screens and grow on larger screens.
- Standardize `--max-content-width` and add consistent safe-area paddings.

### 2. Dashboard Layout Adjustments
#### [MODIFY] `DashboardLayout.css`
- Improve the mobile media queries to ensure the bottom navigation bar doesn't overlap with the main content.
- Reduce `--space-xl` padding on mobile to give more breathing room to cards.

### 3. Data Tables & Lists (Overflow Fixes)
#### [MODIFY] `LeaderboardTable.tsx` / `Leaderboard.css`
- Add `overflow-x: auto` wrappers around tables so they can be swiped horizontally on mobile without breaking the entire page layout.
#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(admin)/admin/students/page.tsx`
- Ensure the admin student table is fully responsive.

### 4. Component Refinements
#### [MODIFY] `Card.tsx` (or related styles)
- Adjust `padding` prop mapping so that `lg` or `xl` padding automatically scales down to `md` or `sm` on mobile viewports.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
- Resize the browser window to mobile width (`< 768px`) and ensure no horizontal scrolling occurs on the main `body`.
- Verify the bottom navigation in the dashboard doesn't hide content.
- Check the Leaderboard and Course Admin pages to ensure tables are swipeable.
